# launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish -- print the loop for DREAM, the dual star, Codex on the pier.
# STATUS -- elder printer, kept as testimony. The living recipe is
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-fleet-chapter.rish dream
# which reads construction/fleet-roster.kyri, so a ship joins, retires, or is renamed in one row
# rather than in a printer of its own (REDS %409). This file keeps every byte it wrote -- it
# carries living and dated references both -- and it names dream in its filename beside an
# astrological MODALITY, `dual`, which named which body orbits which star. That arrangement
# changed and the filename did not, so the breach is one line: a launcher is named for its seat,
# never for its modality. Prepped Class H in construction/SHRED_PREP.md; the cut stays RED until
# Keaton circles it, and the ship name itself is not touched.
#
#
# Dream (night twin Hush) is CODEX IN AI-JAIL ON THE VULTR SEA PIER -- the role swap of
# 20260827.155213 on Keaton's word: the Mind progression proved Codex as a bounded systems
# engineer, and the pier is the Linux metal where Caravan and Tally witnesses actually run, so
# the systems core moved here and the Glow halves moved to Sound and Silence. Dream's lane:
# Caravan and Tally on the microkernel road, the toroidal optimizations, the Scribe seams, and
# the thirty-seat constellation table. The outer jail bounds Codex's inner unrestricted sandbox
# -- the architecture the Mind loop proved on macOS, carried to the pier at its loop-shell rung;
# the full Rishi supervisor with outside signing is the next hardening once Mind's two clone
# commits come home to xy. Charter:
# active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the jail elder the loop wraps must exist.
let elder = run ["test" "-f" "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh"]
assert elder.ok else "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh (the jail elder) is missing"

# invariant: the living charter this star lives in must exist.
let charter = run ["test" "-f" "active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md"]
assert charter.ok else "the six-bodies charter is missing"

say "DREAM -- the dual star of the aether row (night twin Hush), Codex on the pier"
say "============================================================================="
say ""
say "Host: CODEX CLI IN AI-JAIL on the Vultr SEA pier, launched from the outer"
say "terminal. The outer jail is what makes the inner danger-full-access sandbox"
say "safe -- the Mind loop's own architecture, at its loop-shell rung. The shared"
say "discipline lives on the living card; the lane lives in the six-bodies charter."
say ""
say "0a) SURVIVAL: a failed or corrupt pier is never the memory -- the repo is. Reclone from"
say "    xy, re-run this script, paste again; a cut lap costs only its uncommitted work."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per pier: run as a NON-ROOT user; ai-jail GREEN"
say "   (./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh); the codex CLI reachable inside the jail --"
say "   nixos/configuration.nix now DECLARES it (overlay: upstream 0.150.1, the"
say "   prebuilt static-musl binary, past nixos-26.05's source-built 0.133.0), so"
say "   provisioning is one outer-terminal switch rather than a hand-install:"
say "     bash nixos/rebuild-outer.sh   (from this tree's root, ~/grain-dream)"
say "   That runs OUTSIDE the jail -- ai-jail sets no-new-privileges, so sudo and"
say "   nixos-rebuild escalate only from the host shell (gate: provisioning is"
say "   Keaton's hand because it needs sudo, not because the config is missing);"
say "   vendored parity targets:  git submodule update --init --recursive"
say ""
say "1) STATE THAT SURVIVES THE JAIL: nothing to do by hand. agent-jail.sh now"
say "   knows a codex kind, creates .dream-state/codex-home, and maps it onto"
say "   ~/.codex inside the jail -- so --private-home no longer eats the login."
say ""
say "2) LOGIN (once, Keaton's hand -- account auth is custody):"
say "   ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh codex login"
say "   ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh codex login status"
say ""
say "3) SMOKE TEST -- one enclosed answer, seconds:"
say "   (codex 0.150 routes EVERY tool call through its code-mode host binary --"
say "   there is no classic fallback, and disabling the feature fails closed, as"
say "   its own first warning says. The nix overlay installs codex-code-mode-host"
say "   beside codex since the 20260828 rebuild; if this smoke line blocks on a"
say "   missing host, the pier needs that rebuild, never the disable flag)"
say "   ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh codex exec --sandbox danger-full-access 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""

say "4) THE SEAT PROMPT is a file, tools/d/dream_seat_prompt.txt -- never a shell"
say "   string: an apostrophe inside a single-quoted one-liner strands the shell"
say "   at its continuation prompt (Silence hit it first, 20260829)."
say ""
say "   ONE ROUND, ONCE:"
say ""
say "LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh dream"
say ""
say "5) THE 24/7 LOOP -- anchored to the tree that holds the script (~/grain-dream),"
say "   so it can never run against ~/grain-hush beside it; LOOP_HOURS bounds it:"
say ""
say "sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh dream"
say ""
say "6) STREAMING: codex exec already prints human-readable turns, so the tee is"
say "   the whole tail -- session-output/dream.txt, inside the tree."
say ""
say "7) WHY A FILE SENTINEL: the lap echoes its own prompt, which contains the"
say "   words GATES-ONLY, so a grep on the stream would false-stop after one lap."
say "   The lap touches .loop-gates-only only when nothing but gates remains."
say ""
say "8) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- funds and keys, provisioning"
say "   and paying, the maintainer's own identity, and the public seed: never"
say "   publish-seed.sh from this loop, never a force-push of grain-os/grain."
say ""
say "MANY HANDS (granted 20260828, Keaton's word): this seat may spin up multiple"
say "CLI agents inside its own jail and manage them -- parallel codex dependents"
say "dividing a lap's reading or building -- when the split pays. Every standing"
say "law rides into each dependent: custody gates stay MANUAL, one writer per"
say "checkout, and the lap still closes in its one bounded outcome."
say ""
say "GREEN: Dream recipe printed -- the dual star holds the systems core on the metal that proves it."
